0.The x-strips total 11x, so the area is 1x^2+11x+30.3.4 · Expand the side-length expressions to find the rectangle’s area. (x+3)(x+8)Name all four regions: x², qx, px and pq.The four regions are x², 8x, 3x and 24.The x-strips total 11x, so the area is 1x^2+11x+24.3.4 · Expand the side-length expressions to find the rectangle’s area. (x+1)(x+7)Name all four regions: x², qx, px and pq.The four regions are x², 7x, 1x and 7.The x-strips total 8x, so the area is 1x^2+8x+7.3.4 · Expand the side-length expressions to find the rectangle’s area. (x+4)(x+8)Name all four regions: x², qx, px and pq.The four regions are x², 8x, 4x and 32.The x-strips total 12x, so the area is 1x^2+12x+32.3.4 · Expand the side-length expressions to find the rectangle’s area. (x+2)(x+9)Name all four regions: x², qx, px and pq.The four regions are x², 9x, 2x and 18.The x-strips total 11x, so the area is 1x^2+11x+18.3.4 · Expand the side-length expressions to find the rectangle’s area. (x+5)(x+7)Name all four regions: x², qx, px and pq.The four regions are x², 7x, 5x and 35.The x-strips total 12x, so the area is 1x^2+12x+35.3.4 · Expand the side-length expressions to find the rectangle’s area. (x+6)(x+7)Name all four regions: x², qx, px and pq.The four regions are x², 7x, 6x and 42.The x-strips total 13x, so the area is 1x^2+13x+42.3.5 · Factor completely over the integers. 1x^2+7x+10For the monic part, find a pair with product 10 and sum 7.The inner factor pair is 2 and 5.2 + 5 = 7; 2 × 5 = 10.Keep any outside factor: (x+2)(x+5).3.5 · Factor completely over the integers. 1x^2+9x+18For the monic part, find a pair with product 18 and sum 9.The inner factor pair is 3 and 6.3 + 6 = 9; 3 × 6 = 18.Keep any outside factor: (x+3)(x+6).3.5 · Factor completely over the integers. 1x^2-9x+14For the monic part, find a pair with product 14 and sum -9.The inner factor pair is -2 and -7.-2 + -7 = -9; -2 × -7 = 14.Keep any outside factor: (x-2)(x-7).3.5 · Factor completely over the integers. 1x^2+2x-15For the monic part, find a pair with product -15 and sum 2.The inner factor pair is -3 and 5.-3 + 5 = 2; -3 × 5 = -15.Keep any outside factor: (x-3)(x+5).3.5 · Factor completely over the integers. 1x^2-3x-28For the monic part, find a pair with product -28 and sum -3.The inner factor pair is 4 and -7.4 + -7 = -3; 4 × -7 = -28.Keep any outside factor: (x+4)(x-7).3.5 · Factor completely over the integers. 1x^2-10x+24For the monic part, find a pair with product 24 and sum -10.The inner factor pair is -4 and -6.-4 + -6 = -10; -4 × -6 = 24.Keep any outside factor: (x-4)(x-6).3.5 · Factor completely over the integers. 2x^2+18x+16Remove 2 first. For the monic part, find a pair with product 8 and sum 9.The inner factor pair is 1 and 8.1 + 8 = 9; 1 × 8 = 8.Keep any outside factor: 2(x+1)(x+8).3.5 · Factor completely over the integers. 3x^2-9x-30Remove 3 first. For the monic part, find a pair with product -10 and sum -3.The inner factor pair is 2 and -5.2 + -5 = -3; 2 × -5 = -10.Keep any outside factor: 3(x+2)(x-5).3.5 · Factor completely over the integers. 4x^2+40x+84Remove 4 first. For the monic part, find a pair with product 21 and sum 10.The inner factor pair is 3 and 7.3 + 7 = 10; 3 × 7 = 21.Keep any outside factor: 4(x+3)(x+7).3.5 · Factor completely over the integers. 2x^2-20x+32Remove 2 first. For the monic part, find a pair with product 16 and sum -10.The inner factor pair is -2 and -8.-2 + -8 = -10; -2 × -8 = 16.Keep any outside factor: 2(x-2)(x-8).3.5 · Factor completely over the integers. 1x^2+10x+25For the monic part, find a pair with product 25 and sum 10.The inner factor pair is 5 and 5.5 + 5 = 10; 5 × 5 = 25.Keep any outside factor: (x+5)(x+5).3.5 · Factor completely over the integers. 1x^2+0x-36For the monic part, find a pair with product -36 and sum 0.The inner factor pair is -6 and 6.-6 + 6 = 0; -6 × 6 = -36.Keep any outside factor: (x-6)(x+6).3.6 · Factor completely over the integers. 2x^2+7x+3Find two coefficients with product 6 and sum 7.The middle terms can have coefficients 6 and 1.They add to 7 and multiply to 6.Grouping gives (2x+1)(1x+3). Expand to check.3.6 · Factor completely over the integers. 6x^2+17x+5Find two coefficients with product 30 and sum 17.The middle terms can have coefficients 15 and 2.They add to 17 and multiply to 30.Grouping gives (3x+1)(2x+5). Expand to check.3.6 · Factor completely over the integers. 6x^2+17x+12Find two coefficients with product 72 and sum 17.The middle terms can have coefficients 8 and 9.They add to 17 and multiply to 72.Grouping gives (2x+3)(3x+4). Expand to check.3.6 · Factor completely over the integers. 3x^2+13x-10Find two coefficients with product -30 and sum 13.The middle terms can have coefficients 15 and -2.They add to 13 and multiply to -30.Grouping gives (3x-2)(1x+5). Expand to check.3.6 · Factor completely over the integers. 6x^2-7x-3Find two coefficients with product -18 and sum -7.The middle terms can have coefficients 2 and -9.They add to -7 and multiply to -18.Grouping gives (2x-3)(3x+1). Expand to check.3.6 · Factor completely over the integers. 4x^2-11x-3Find two coefficients with product -12 and sum -11.The middle terms can have coefficients -12 and 1.They add to -11 and multiply to -12.Grouping gives (4x+1)(1x-3). Expand to check.3.6 · Factor completely over the integers. 10x^2+9x+2Find two coefficients with product 20 and sum 9.The middle terms can have coefficients 5 and 4.They add to 9 and multiply to 20.Grouping gives (5x+2)(2x+1). Expand to check.3.6 · Factor completely over the integers. 6x^2-11x+3Find two coefficients with product 18 and sum -11.The middle terms can have coefficients -9 and -2.They add to -11 and multiply to 18.Grouping gives (3x-1)(2x-3). Expand to check.3.6 · Factor completely over the integers. 2x^2+13x+20Find two coefficients with product 40 and sum 13.The middle terms can have coefficients 8 and 5.They add to 13 and multiply to 40.Grouping gives (2x+5)(1x+4). Expand to check.3.6 · Factor completely over the integers. 12x^2+5x-2Find two c